# CLAUDE.md — CityFurnish Operations Dashboard

Project memory for Claude Code. Read this first before making changes.

---

## What this is

Single-page operations dashboard for CityFurnish furniture rental ops. One ~30 MB HTML file (`Task_Efficiency_Dashboard.html`) with all data baked in as JS globals. Refreshed periodically by a Python script that pulls from Metabase + Mongo.

- **Live URL:** https://adityakumarcf.github.io/cityfurnish-ops-dashboard/Task_Efficiency_Dashboard.html
- **Repo:** https://github.com/adityakumarCF/cityfurnish-ops-dashboard
- **Password gate:** `cf@admin` (sessionStorage)
- **Hosting:** GitHub Pages, auto-deploys on push to `main`

---

## Tabs

1. Overview · 2. Task Efficiency · 3. FAD Analysis · 4. FSD Analysis · 5. TAT Performance · 6. Trip Efficiency · 7. KPI Trend · 8. Benchmark · 9. Action Needed · 10. Simplified

Page anchors use `id="page-<key>"`. Render functions are `render<Key>Page()`. Data refreshed via `rerender(<key>)`.

---

## Critical conventions (don't violate)

- **Cities:** Allowed = `Bangalore, Gurgaon, Hyderabad, Mumbai, Pune` only. Enforced in Python (`ALLOWED_CITIES`) and JS (`CITIES_ALLOWED`).
- **Excluded job types:** `PO Payment, Stock Transfer, Refurb Transfer`. Filtered during Python build.
- **Thursdays excluded** from all aggregation. Use `isThursdayYMD(sd)`.
- **Reschedule == FSD Missed:** `r[FSD] === 'False' || r[FSD] === 'NoFS'`. NoFS (Pending) counts as missed because the date commitment was missed. Used everywhere — TAT, KPI Trend, FSD page, drills, Reschedule Reason Breakdown, Top Offenders.
- **FAD uniqueness:** Delivery/SR use full-history OID counts. **Pickup uses rolling 2-month window** (previous month start → max scheduled date).
- **Vehicle-days, not unique fleet:** Done Efficiency, capacity, FAD/FSD vehicle tables all use vehicle-days (`Σ_day unique vehicles in city`). Otherwise weekly/monthly tables don't scale.

