## Don't refactor without explicit approval

This session burned through 3 wasted iterations because the assistant redesigned instead of augmenting. **Default behavior:**
1. Sketch the change in text
2. Share a mockup if visual
3. Wait for explicit approval
4. Then build — additively, not by replacing existing UI

The user has explicitly protected:
- City × Category Leaders section on KPI Trend (don't touch its data, structure, or formatting)
- Existing drill modal infra
- Excel exports
- Manager / Simplified view

---

## Component conventions (KPI Trend tab)

The KPI Trend tab uses **one comparison-table component**: `compCard9(title, mrows, firstColLabel)`.

- Builds 9 columns: `<First> | Day | Yest. | 7d Avg | 30d Avg | Δ d-1 | Δ 7d | Δ 30d | Verdict`
- Auto-generates an insight strip from `mrows` (biggest drop, biggest gain, X of Y declining/improving)
- Each row built via `mRow(label, vA, vB, v7, v30, isPct, hb, dec, metricKey)`

Don't add a parallel table component unless the data shape is fundamentally different (like the City × Category Leaders matrix).

